        {
          "type": "kotak",
          "title": "Te means both hot and spicy",
          "items": [
            "Irish doesn't separate hot in temperature from hot in taste; both are *te*, just as in English. So *Tá an tae te* (\"the tea is hot\") and *Tá an bia te* (\"the food is spicy\") use the same word.",
            "If you need to be clear, add a phrase: *te ó spíosraí* (\"hot from spices\") or *róthe le hithe* (\"too hot to eat\").",
            "Irish food is rarely spicy, so if you say *Is maith liom bia te*, your host will most likely warm up your plate."
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
